        "text": "The lecture now develops Boundaries of public diplomacy. The framework distinguishes Related term, How it differs, Where overlap may occur, and Conventional diplomacy. Because propaganda and public diplomacy can use the same media, their boundary should be assessed through purpose, source transparency, truthfulness and selectivity, audience agency, reciprocity and feedback rather than medium alone. It differs from traditional diplomacy in primary interlocutors rather than in complete separation: ministries and embassies still matter, yet students, journalists, specialists, cultural organisations, diasporas, businesses and civic groups may become audiences, intermediaries or co-producers. When comparing public diplomacy with propaganda, do not rely on tone alone. Propaganda is systematic communication intended to direct perception and behaviour towards a political purpose."
