        "text": "Cull’s five functions marks the next step in the analysis. The framework separates listening, advocacy, cultural diplomacy, exchange, and international broadcasting as related but distinct functions. Operational instruments include policy explanation and advocacy, international broadcasting, digital communication, cultural presentation, educational exchange, professional networks and listening. A broadcast may provide credible information, prime an agenda or merely signal presence; an exchange may transfer knowledge, generate interpersonal trust or function chiefly as a funded opportunity. Listening becomes consequential only if information from foreign publics enters organisational learning or changes communication, programme design or policy advice. One-way transmission may sometimes meet a limited informational purpose, whereas reciprocity may be essential for a long-term relationship."
