        "text": "Light Reading and Viewing Package connects the lecture to the assigned evidence and preparation. Additional: Selected chapter from Liping Bu, Making the World Like Us. In Schindler’s account of early public–private partnerships, this longer horizon distinguishes exchange from a publicity campaign seeking immediate assent. It is an organised encounter in which participants gain access to another society, learn through sustained contact and form relationships that may outlast the programme itself. Educational exchange is more than the movement of students or academics across borders. This standard treats participants as thinking partners rather than as containers for a national message."
