        "title": "Flashcard round 1: date and actor",
        "text": "Flashcard round 1: date and actor checks whether the central distinction can be applied accurately. The guiding question is: Question: When and in what context was the CPI established? When the United States entered the First World War in April 1917, the Wilson administration confronted linked domestic and international communication problems. President Woodrow Wilson created the Committee on Public Information and appointed journalist George Creel as its chairman. The committee connected information, persuasion and mobilisation, presenting the war as a contest over political principles as well as military power. Its work shows how communication becomes part of governing during an emergency rather than an activity added after policy has been made."
